==========================================================================
MEASURED cost of the C_b route against the stored B x B control
==========================================================================
The sum(e^3)/B^3 ratios of 105x to 4159x are a COUNT of elimination
multiply-adds, NOT a wall-time prediction.  This folder's last
cube-law extrapolation (a two-point B^3.50 fit) under-called the
(k = 4, n = 7) factorisation by 1.6x, against a shape-matched estimate
that landed within 0.6%.  The cost below is END TO END and INCLUDES
building the slices, which cost 283 s on its own at n = 6.  If the
slice build dominates, the win is single-digit and that is the result.

NOT evidence for the n-uniform theorem: at these n the Gram is already
known positive definite, so C_b coming out definite is a consequence.
==========================================================================

